Modern theme, quick actions, history persistence, inline HTML rendering

Four feature additions in a single batch.

1. Sun Valley dark theme (sv_ttk) applied across the dashboard. Tk frames,
buttons and labels converted to ttk widgets so the theme styles them.
The transcript Text widget keeps custom dark colors (bg #1e1e1e, role-
tagged fg). Bumped fonts to 13 pt for Gujarati body text, 15 pt bold
title, for readability.

2. Quick-action button row above the entry box: chart-from-xlsx, list
files, scaffold React app, deploy to Vercel, push to GitHub, plus a
Clear button that wipes the visible transcript. One click fills the
entry with a Gujarati prompt template the user can tweak before sending.

3. Conversation history persistence (new history.py module):
   - Saves last 100 transcript entries plus the observed Claude
     session_id to ~/.gujarati_claude_history.json on shutdown.
   - On launch, the previous transcript is replayed into the GUI behind
     a "previous / new conversation" header, AND the bridge passes
     --resume <session_id> so Claude itself keeps the multi-turn
     context, not just the visual lines.
   - ClaudeBridge now captures session_id from the first system/init
     stream event and exposes it via observed_session_id.

4. Inline HTML and SVG rendering in the outputs pane via tkinterweb:
   - When Claude saves an .html, .htm, or .svg artifact to outputs/,
     it renders inline in the right pane (no need to alt-tab to a
     browser).
   - Image preview (PIL) and HTML render (HtmlFrame) coexist in a
     swap-on-select container.
   - Graceful fallback to the "open in OS app" placeholder if
     tkinterweb is missing.

setup_text.bat updated to install the new deps sv-ttk and tkinterweb
into the gc311 conda env alongside the existing data stack.

Tests: 31 of 34 pass, same Windows POSIX-path failures we already
documented in Ultraplan's tests. No new regressions.
